The CLI execution block does not exit with a non-zero exit code when the validation status is anything other than a successful pass (e.g., 'fail'). This violates the general rule requiring CLI validation scripts to exit with a non-zero exit code for non-pass statuses to prevent silent failures in CI/CD pipelines.

